 under the [`preview`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#format_preview) flag, promoting them to stable through minor releases, in accordance with our [versioning policy](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/discussions/6998#discussioncomment-7016766).
 
+#### Fluent call chains split before the first call
+
+When a call chain is formatted in fluent style, Ruff breaks the chain before the first call or
+subscript rather than before the second one. For example, in preview mode, a chain that doesn't
+fit on a single line is split as:
+
+```python
+obj
+    .first_call()
+    .second_call()
+```
+
+rather than keeping `obj.first_call()` together on the first line. Consecutive calls and
+subscripts on a single object are treated as one unit, and a parenthesized root counts as one
+call-like element even if it isn't itself a call or subscript. This only affects preview mode;
+stable formatting is unchanged.
+
 ### F-string formatting
 
 _Stabilized in Ruff 0.9.0_
